<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan cotton output reaches 8.58 million bales.</title>
<headline>Pakistan cotton output reaches 8.58 million bales.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The state-run Cotton Export Corporation of Pakistan (CEC) said on Friday 1996/97 (July-June) cotton output had reached a provisional 8.58 million 375-lb bales, down from 9.788 million in the year-ago period.</p>
<p>Delivery and ginning figures in million bales (year-ago):</p>
<p>		    Punjab	   Sindh	    Total</p>
<p> Delivery	 6.519 (8.063)  2.061 (1.724)  8.580 (9.788)</p>
<p> Pressed	  6.458 (8.018)  1.988 (1.662)  8.446 (9.681)</p>
<p> Mill sales     5.306 (6.329)  1.728 (1.154)  7.035 (7.764)</p>
<p> Export sales   0.005 (0.944)  0.0004(0.386)  0.0054(1.331)</p>
<p> CEC		nil   (nil)    nil   (nil)    nil   (nil)</p>
<p> Unsold	   1.207 (0.789)  0.332 (0.183)  1.539 (0.972)</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
